# Installer error output (2026-09)

The public installer exited with status 141 and no message at `==> Base packages` when a package was already installed. `apt-cache policy | awk ... exit` closed the pipe; `pipefail` treated that as a fatal error.

## Change

- Read the full apt policy without closing the pipe early.
- On any unexpected failure, print the line number, status, and command, then exit.
- Avoid the same pipe close when checking privileged groups.
